# Python environment
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Large fixture artifacts: re-derivable from the spec's seeds by
# corpora/build_fixture.py, and their digests are committed in MANIFEST.sha256.
# Small artifacts (MANIFEST.sha256, characterization.json, query_ids.json,
# ground_truth.npy) ARE committed.
fixtures/*/vectors.npy
fixtures/*/projection.npy
fixtures/*/sample.jsonl.zst

# Model caches (weights are pinned by sha256 in the fixture spec, not vendored)
.cache/
hf_cache/
models_cache/
.huggingface/
sentence_transformers_cache/
logs/
*.bundle

# Pod session records (task 006). Pod ids, start times and the rate agreed at
# confirmation — local bookkeeping, not receipts, and never the API key.
.oneground/

# VS Code workspace files — local editor state, not project configuration.
*.code-workspace

# Packaging.
*.egg-info/

# Run outputs. NARROWED IN TASK 044i, and the reason is the root cause of a
# live defect rather than housekeeping.
#
# This was a blanket `runs/`, written to keep bulk out -- the arxiv-150k run
# alone is 1.4 MB of sample ids. It also kept out `report.json` and
# `verify.json`, which are a few tens of KB and are **the receipts a published
# decision rests on**. The consequence was found on the lab page: its verdict
# came from a verify run whose receipts were never committed, so the decision
# the page showed could not be re-derived by anyone, and when a later run
# disagreed nothing could reconcile them. A rule written to keep bulk out kept
# out the evidence.
#
# So: the small receipts that make a decision re-derivable are COMMITTED, and
# the bulk is not. The test is size and re-derivability -- a file that is
# large and rebuildable from its seeds stays out; a file that is small and is
# the only record of a measurement goes in.
runs/**
!runs/
!runs/*/
!runs/*/*/
!runs/*/report.json
!runs/*/verify.json
!runs/*/verify_info.json
!runs/*/simulate.json
!runs/*/simulate_info.json
!runs/*/build_info.json
!runs/*/characterization.json
!runs/*/manifest.yaml
!runs/*/MANIFEST.sha256
!runs/*/queries_ids.json
# Proposal cards sit at runs/<run>/proposals/<name>/, one level deeper.
!runs/*/*/*/
!runs/*/*/*/card.json
!runs/*/*/*/prediction.json
!runs/*/*/*/propose_info.json
!runs/*/*/*/MANIFEST.sha256
# A NOTE ON THE RECEIPTS ALREADY IN `runs/` WHEN THIS RULE CHANGED.
# Narrowing this made about 110 existing files trackable, and they must not be
# bulk-added: they predate task 044g's path fix, so they carry absolute paths
# through a home directory, and committing them would put 95+ machine
# identifiers into the tracked tree. `test_no_tracked_file_carries_a_machine_
# identifier` catches that, which is the guard working rather than a trap --
# it failed on exactly this during 044i and the commit was undone.
#
# So this rule is forward-looking: receipts written from now on are clean at
# their write site and are kept. A historical receipt that a page cites is
# copied into `fixtures/<id>/report/` instead, curated and named for what it
# is -- core's second option, and the route the 9 September superseded report
# took.
#
# Still out, and each for its size rather than its kind: sample_ids.json is
# 1.3 MB of ids re-derivable from the sampling seed; ground truth, vectors and
# projections are megabytes and rebuildable; report.html is a rendering of
# report.json; state/ is the simulator's emitted arrays.
runs/*/sample_ids.json
runs/*/report.html
runs/*/state/
runs/**/*.npy
runs/**/*.bin
runs/**/*.tgz
runs/**/*.parquet

# Calibration fixture arrays (task 012): 486 MB total and re-derivable by
# anyone from the upstream ANN-Benchmarks HDF5, whose sha256 is recorded in
# fixtures/glove-100-angular.fixture.yaml. Scoped to this fixture on purpose:
# arxiv-smoke's queries.npy is small and IS committed.
# (vectors.npy is already covered by the fixtures/*/vectors.npy rule above.)
fixtures/glove-100-angular/queries.npy
fixtures/glove-100-angular/ground_truth.npy
fixtures/glove-100-angular/ground_truth_distances.npy

# Built HNSW indexes parked by `calibrate curve` (task 012b). ~600 MB each and
# rebuildable, but a rebuild is 69 minutes -- the cache exists so a failure in
# the two-minute search after it does not throw that away. Under .cache/,
# which is already ignored; named here so the reason is on the record.

# Build artifacts. `python -m build` writes these; they are re-derivable and
# the release attaches the ones the developer built, not whatever is on disk.
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# Scratch scripts. docs/RELEASE.md section 6 publishes the briefs and the
# reports -- the receipt trail, including the runs that failed -- and keeps
# the working itself in archive/private-history. These are the working: one
# shot text patches, API probes, log captures, the harnesses a measurement was
# taken with. A report names the script a number came from; the script is not
# part of what ships.
tasks/scratch/

# The CI-only corpus and requirements the calibration workflow generates.
# Re-derivable from .github/scripts/make_ci_corpus.py and its seed.
.ci/

# sec-filings-10k ships its corpus and its query vectors as a release asset:
# documents.jsonl.zst is 692 MB and queries.npy is 6 MB. Scoped to this fixture
# on purpose, for the same reason glove's rules are: arxiv-smoke's queries.npy
# is small and IS committed, and a blanket fixtures/*/queries.npy would
# silently contradict that.
fixtures/sec-filings-10k/documents.jsonl.zst
fixtures/sec-filings-10k/queries.npy

# Session tarballs fetched into the repo root; their contents are extracted
# beside them and committed, the archive itself is not.
/*-small.tgz
